{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's own trace places him 156.99 m from the pickup pin at his closest recorded approach anywhere in the 69-fix run - outside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius that POL-NS-02 fixes for this zone class, but far inside the 400 m ceiling POL-NS-03 sets for a wrong-face-of-venue arrival. The rider's own account ('he stayed on the other side and cancelled') describes exactly that situation, not an abandoned job, so the driver attended the venue and the case is decided under POL-NS-03 rather than as a driver who never came.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (a) of POL-NS-01 is satisfied and the driver's cancellation was not premature in time on the platform's own clock: the trip record carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 20:28:14 and the cancellation at 20:32:36, an elapsed wait of 4.4 minutes (262 seconds) against the 180 second free_wait_sec in force for this trip under platform_policy. The driver gave the rider substantially longer than the free waiting period the fee pays for, whatever the geofence arithmetic finally shows.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-05 catches a false arrival marker only where the fix matched to the arrival timestamp puts the driver more than 300 m from the pin or travelling at 15 km/h or more. Neither trigger is made out on this record: the driver's closest fix anywhere in the trace is 156.99 m from the pin, inside the 300 m leash, and the trace contains stationary 0.0 km/h samples. No false-arrival finding or POL-NS-05(ii) referral should be recorded against this driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's POL-NS-04 route fails at limb (b). The rider's locating message was sent at 20:28:34 and the driver replied 'ok' at 20:29:04 - thirty seconds later, and read at 20:29:14 - well inside the 120 second window limb (b) allows. The driver neither ignored the message nor left it unanswered, so the rider cannot be exonerated on a driver coordination failure and the case must be decided on the arrival and dwell arithmetic.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no farming pattern and no escalation ground on the profiles. The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check requires driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d of 4 or more AND a rate above 0.08; this driver shows 2 terminations against 87 completed trips in the same window, a rate of 0.023, so the check does not trip. The lifetime counter prior_no_show_flags is not the trailing-30-day field the clause names and may not be substituted for it, and both parties' disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0, so POL-NS-09(c) is not engaged either.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02711", "EV-RPROF-02711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in the bundle is impaired and the disputed amount is clean. Every artifact is COMPLETE at weight 1.0; the GPS trace carries 100.0 percent coverage, a 10 second cadence and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds, so the POL-NS-08(a) clock-skew, (b) trace-defect and (c) chat-defect limbs are not engaged and no POL-NS-09(e) escalation arises; and the fare breakdown's cancellation-fee line of 4.50 SGD reconciles exactly with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of 4.50, so POL-NS-08(d) is satisfied and the amount itself is not in issue. On a clean record the single live question is whether the fee is chargeable at all.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02711", "EV-FARE-02711", "EV-TRIP-02711"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fee_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both parties: the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee charged on TRP-02711 is refunded in full to the rider. No driver compensation is payable, and the case is not escalated.\n\nWhy the fee does not stand. The driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-02711: 69 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps) never places the vehicle inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius of the pickup pin at Blk 231 Serangoon Ave 3; his closest approach anywhere in the trip was 156.99 m (derived.driver_track.min_distance_m), and the derived arrival block reports 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes and no continuous in-geofence run. The rider's device, by contrast, lies within 14.78 m of the pin across all 47 of its fixes (20:26:34-20:33:28). POL-NS-01 limb (b) therefore fails: the 20:28:14 'arrived' event is a driver button press (platform_policy.arrival_marker = BUTTON), and a pressed marker establishes arrival only if the trace corroborates it (POL-NS-02; POL-NS-12 covers GPS_AUTO arrivals only and is unavailable here by its own terms). POL-NS-01 limb (c) runs the waiting clock from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from the tap, so the required 180 s dwell (platform_policy.free_wait_sec) never began: measured dwell 0.0 s against a 180.0 s minimum. POL-NS-06 makes the fee refundable on that shortfall whether or not the rider was present, and limb (d) cannot be satisfied because the dwell it measures never elapsed. The driver's 262-second wait on the trip-record clock (20:28:14 to 20:32:36) is not in-geofence waiting time and does not change this outcome.\n\nPOL-NS-03. The driver's case that this is a wrong-face-of-venue arrival is geometrically available (156.99 m is inside the 400 m ceiling), but it yields the same fee outcome: POL-NS-03 also refunds the cancellation fee in full. It matters only to compensation, and limb (i) decides that against the driver: the rider stated her sub-location in the chat log at 20:28:34 ('im at the main entrance next to the taxi stand, block A', EV-CHAT-02711), the driver read it and replied 'ok' at 20:29:04, and the trace never shows him closing the last 157 m before cancelling at 20:32:36. POL-NS-03(ii)'s platform-funded goodwill is not available: it requires registered_pickup_points of 2 or more (this trip has 1) and no sub-location stated by either party.\n\nOther claims. POL-NS-05 is not engaged - the driver never came within 300 m of the pin - so no false-arrival finding and no POL-NS-05(ii) referral is recorded. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider (the driver replied 30 seconds after her message, inside limb (b)'s 120-second window), but the refund does not rest on it. POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is unavailable: EV-ADVIS-02711-01 is MISSING and carries weight 0.0, so it carries no fact and neither raises nor lowers the 180-second minimum. POL-NS-07 compensation is not payable because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full; in any event the anti-farming check does not trip (2 no-show terminations against 87 completed trips in 30 days, rate 0.023, against thresholds of 4 and 0.08 - lifetime counters such as prior_no_show_flags are context only and were not used). The driver's statement that he 'was at the pickup as shown on the map' is a party statement carrying no weight; it is contradicted by his own trace and establishes no fact.\n\nIntegrity and escalation. Nothing is impaired under POL-NS-08: no clock skew (the 20:28:14 arrival stamp falls exactly on a fix), no gap over 120 s, 69 fixes in the window, the chat log's 2 messages match trip_record.chat_message_count, and the fare's 4.50 cancellation-fee line reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: the apparent conflict between the button press and the trace is resolved by POL-NS-01(b) and POL-NS-02; neither profile shows disputes with the other party in 90 days; and the deciding fact rests on weight-1.0 artifacts.\n\nConfidence. The deciding fact - the driver's position and in-geofence dwell - is carried by EV-GPS-02711 at weight 1.0, so POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at 1.0; I set it at 0.95. The refund of SGD 4.50 is below POL-GEN-05's execution threshold of SGD 8.00 and executes automatically. This is a provisional ruling; either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
